{"id":"cyberminimalism","title":"Cyberminimalism","url":"https://aesthetics.fandom.com/wiki/Cyberminimalism","rev":237917,"fetched":"2026-10-16","lead":[{"t":"p","c":[{"t":"b","c":["Cyberminimalism"]}," (or ",{"t":"b","c":["Cyberbougie"]},") is a hyper-minimalistic aesthetic that arose in the late 2010s. It pushed beyond ",{"t":"a","c":["Flat Design"],"id":"flat-design"},"'s minimalism into an even more reductive design style. At its most extreme, it is composed of sans-serif words, color gradients, a design grid and little to nothing else. Originally confined to the web and tech spaces, it later spread into other industries."]}],"sections":[{"title":"Visuals","id":"visuals","blocks":[{"t":"p","c":["Common visuals include:"]},{"t":"ul","items":[{"c":["Extreme emphasis on a certain form of \"sleekness\""]},{"c":["Usually ",{"t":"a","c":["Flat Design"],"id":"flat-design"}," principles in UI elements, but ",{"t":"a","c":["Neumorphism"],"id":"neumorphism"}," and ",{"t":"a","c":["Glassmorphism"],"id":"glassmorphism"}," are also possible"]},{"c":["Black or white (rarely colored) text"]},{"c":["Sans-Serif and grotesque fonts"]},{"c":["Slab serifs"]},{"c":["Gradients, both normal and grainy"]},{"c":["Simple, symmetrical geometric shapes likes squares and circles"]},{"c":["Bento-style grids (especially after their popularization by Apple in 2022)"]}]}]},{"title":"Gallery","id":"gallery","blocks":[{"t":"gallery","items":[{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/d/d8/Datalands_landing_page_design_%282019%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240529043652","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Datalands landing page design, 2019"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/c/cd/Delegated_app_branding_%282019%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240529043652","w":185,"h":185,"cap":["Delegated (app) branding, 2019"]},{"src":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/aesthetics/images/1/1b/The_Pillars_of_Wellbeing_%282020%29.jpg/revision/latest?cb=20240529043653","w":185,"h":185,"cap"